@@ -577,3 +577,22 @@ built desktop, Host, CLI and actual AI SDK stream path. The Chinese/English mess
 missing subscription service access, retains HTTP 403, marks the probe failed and leaves metadata
 closed. A complete synthetic successful stream marks only its tested model successful. Original
 review-profile credentials, default and model parameters are preserved; no paid probe was sent.
+
+### Product identity and subscription tiers
+
+Keep the existing vendor/service/region catalog and credential owner. Within an intake section,
+a vendor group containing one named service uses that product's public service name; multi-service
+groups retain the vendor heading and existing service selector. Generic API groups keep vendor
+identity. Grok subscription uses its own Grok asset and label, while xAI API retains xAI. Membership
+tiers belong to each authenticated account; do not create duplicate login routes per tier or infer
+entitlement from the tier label. Preserve user-authored connection aliases and stable route IDs.
+
+The official Grok Build billing extension enriches credits with RemoteSettings.subscription_tier_display
+(or subscription_tier). Read /settings and /billing?format=credits concurrently with the same saved
+account headers and bounded transport, through the existing subscription usage/cache owner. Only the
+whitelisted tier string is projected; remote settings cannot change Fleet behavior. Missing quota
+with a known tier remains unknown quota, never full/zero. A usage period end is not a membership
+expiry or paid billing period. Keep unknown future tier names rather than mapping them to Free.
+Reuse the existing account badge and original plan-status card; known tiers receive established
+semantic color tokens. Original ProviderDetailFeedback and SectionLayout remain byte-identical to
+the pin; only failure copy/classification/manual dismissal differs from upstream.
